                    {
                        "sense_id": "720b91a3-1f64-3042-9e11-0007561b6419",
                        "entry_id": "a2b5a328-6f31-332d-92a7-6c310c08fdce",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various insects, including the silverfish and firebrats, of the order Thysanura (now Zygentoma), which have three long caudal filaments."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "782f2e3d-e17f-4b3f-ad1e-d225913b30cd",
                                "sense_id": "720b91a3-1f64-3042-9e11-0007561b6419",
                                "text": "The best known and most often seen thysanurans are the two domesticated species: silverfish and firebrat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6c6ddfd-f73c-4c3b-bffa-96714fd88465",
                                "sense_id": "720b91a3-1f64-3042-9e11-0007561b6419",
                                "text": "As insects go, thysanurans are about as primitive as an arthropod can get and still be considered an insect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cef407fa-7058-4c13-bd54-fe09b62d8df5",
                                "sense_id": "720b91a3-1f64-3042-9e11-0007561b6419",
                                "text": "2008, Timothy J. Bradley, Saline-water Insects: Ecology, Physiology and Evolution, Jill Lancaster, Robert A. Briers, Aquatic Insects: Challenges to Populations: Proceedings of the Royal Entomological Society's 24th Symposium, page 22,\nMarine thysanurans are another abundant and highly successful group of apterygotes able to exploit the ocean shore."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
